  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-tiered mechanism that ultimately targets prostate cells. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for Racotumomab, a drug that in turn targets prostate cells. This indicates a direct interaction between Mollicellin N and the prostate cell lineage, potentially through the Racotumomab pathway. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also shown to target GDM-1 and P2X purinoceptor 1, which are implicated in cellular signaling and function. These targets may contribute to the observed effects on prostate cells, though the exact mechanism by which these targets influence prostate cell behavior remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Mollicellin N and prostate cells, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the specific molecular interactions that underlie this relationship.",
